Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the pool on exec_server's file port, EXEC_FILE_THREADS threads, so that one execve held on a file does not hold the next.  With one thread a load waits for every load before it, and mount_test's [32] has a load of /hello_exec wait behind one of /mount_test/stall, which the liar holds at its open until the arm lets it go after 30 s.
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: mount_test: \[32\] WRONG — a load of /hello_exec not back in 30 s, one of /mount_test/stall held at this mount's open: exec_server's file loads wait for each other; let go, the first came back \(-1\), the second came back \(0\)
Note: every other file load asked of exec_server in those 30 s waits too; the image port keeps its own thread.

